%description:

A deviation of the TR 36.873 UMa environment height from the specification,
recorded rather than fixed (model deviation 26). TR 36.873 v12.7.0 Table
7.2-1 NOTE 4 draws h_E = 1 m with probability 1/(1+C(d2D, hUT)), with the
C(d2D, hUT) of Table 7.2-2, which has a distance term; so does the model's
own UMa LOS probability. Tr36873PathLossModel::drawEnvironmentHeight() takes
C without it, ((hUT-13)/10)^1.5, so the probability of 1 m does not depend on
the distance: at hUT = 22.5 m it is 0.52 everywhere, where the specification
gives 0.98 at 30 m, 0.63 at 100 m and 0.29 at 200 m.

Graded from the frequencies of 40000 draws, as in PathLossEnvironmentHeight,
which pins the current distribution. When fixed, drop the %expected-failure
line, fold the cases into PathLossEnvironmentHeight and drop the pin there.

%expected-failure: the TR 36.873 h_E draw leaves out the distance term of C(d2D, hUT)

%includes:
#include <map>
#include "PathLossTestUtil.h"
#include "simu5g/stack/phy/channelmodel/Tr36873PathLossModel.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;

%activity:
CaseRecorder probe(this, 1e-6);
const int N = 40000;
const double heValues[] = { 1, 12, 15, 18, 21 };

ScenarioParams p;
p.scenario = URBAN_MACROCELL;
p.hNodeB = 25;
p.hUe = 22.5;
p.carrierFrequencyGHz = 0.8;
Tr36873PathLossModel m;
p.apply(m, this);

for (double d : { 30.0, 100.0, 200.0 }) {
    std::map<double, int> counts;
    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++)
        counts[m.drawEnvironmentHeight(d)]++;
    for (double v : heValues)
        probe.record("t873_p_he", p, { { "d2D", d }, { "hE", v } }, counts[v] / (double)N, 0.01);
}

probe.summary();

%postrun-command: ../../pathloss_reference.py --grade test.out >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=15 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
